column5:
Changed NFmiGrid::Coverage method to use non latlon converting method:
if (theGrid.itsArea->IsInside(GridToLatLon(x, y)))
==>
if (theGrid.itsArea->IsInsideWorldXY(GridToWorldXY(x, y)))

Fixed deallocation of previous NFmiQueryInfo object

clang++ --analyze warning:

newbase/NFmiSnapShotInterface.cpp:119:25: warning: Dereference of null pointer (loaded from variable 'theInfo')
  if (itsInfo) *theInfo = new NFmiQueryInfo(*itsInfo);
                ~~~~~~~ ^
newbase/NFmiSnapShotInterface.cpp:119:25: warning: Use of memory after it is freed
  if (itsInfo) *theInfo = new NFmiQueryInfo(*itsInfo);
               ~~~~~~~~ ^

theInfo is a pointer to a pointer. The error is caused by a previous line

    if (theInfo) delete theInfo;

Fixed the code to

    if (*theInfo) delete *theInfo;

In NFmiProj::InverseProjStr method fixed
    if (ints.find(name_value.first) == keepers.end())
==>
    if (ints.find(name_value.first) == ints.end())
, wrong set's end iterator used to test find result.

Fixed NFmiStringTools::Split function to with lists of numbers that have spaces after number by trimming the right side of constructed substrings. Following code would throw exception before this fix:

auto numbers = NFmiStringTools::Split<std::vector<int>>("1,2 ,3", ",");

The space after number 2 would cause the exception. If spaces are before numbers that was no problem like in this example:

auto numbers = NFmiStringTools::Split<std::vector<int>>("1, 2, 3", ",");

Changed NFmiGrid::Coverage method to use non latlon converting method:
if (theGrid.itsArea->IsInside(GridToLatLon(x, y)))
==>
if (theGrid.itsArea->IsInsideWorldXY(GridToWorldXY(x, y)))

Added possibility to memory map a new writeable querydata file

Sample code:

int main()
{
  // Memory map a sample input file
  NFmiQueryData qd("input.sqd");
  NFmiFastQueryInfo src(&qd);

  // Make a copy with all data points set to a missing value
  NFmiQueryData* out1 = NFmiQueryDataUtil::CreateEmptyData(src, "missing.sqd", true);

  // Make a copy with all data points zeroed out
  NFmiQueryData* out2 = NFmiQueryDataUtil::CreateEmptyData(src, "zeros.sqd", false);

  // Make a copy of the original
  NFmiQueryData* out3 = NFmiQueryDataUtil::CreateEmptyData(src, "copy.sqd", false);
  NFmiFastQueryInfo dst(out3);
  for (src.ResetParam(), dst.ResetParam(); src.NextParam() && dst.NextParam();)
    for (src.ResetLocation(), dst.ResetLocation(); src.NextLocation() && dst.NextLocation();)
      for (src.ResetLevel(), dst.ResetLevel(); src.NextLevel() && dst.NextLevel();)
        for (src.ResetTime(), dst.ResetTime(); src.NextTime() && dst.NextTime();)
          dst.FloatValue(src.FloatValue());

  delete out1;
  delete out2;
  delete out3;

  return 0;
}

[CoreEngine] Refactor launch CLIs:
1. Added the CLI to show the job list (fedml launch job log), cancel the job (fedml launch cancel), show the job queue (fedml launch queue);
2. Refactor the falcon login CLI (fedml falcon login) to launch login (fedml launch login);
3. Refactor the falcon logout CLI (fedml falcon logout) to launch logout (fedml launch logout);
4. Saved the API key when running the CLI successfully;
5. Added the -h option for all CLI commands to show help texts.

Changed NFmiGrid::Coverage method to use non latlon converting method:
if (theGrid.itsArea->IsInside(GridToLatLon(x, y)))
==>
if (theGrid.itsArea->IsInsideWorldXY(GridToWorldXY(x, y)))

